docs/review-remaining-2026-10-12/validation/source-reports/codeshell-remaining-cli-chat-report.md:213:**chat — source-directed:** all12 adapter production files `telegram,discord,slack,lark,dingtalk,wecom,wechat,matrix,mattermost,line,whatsapp,teams`; `src/{channel,adapter-factory,chat-gateway,delivery-queue,cli,gateway,bound-session-chat,ingress,attachments,lifecycle,media,webhook,config,desktop-control-client,instance-lock,notification-relay,notification-progress,wechat-storage,wechat-login,service-manager,codeshell}.ts`. Actual pre-load sender filtering was checked at adapter construction and adapter handlers: allowlist middleware is gateway dispatch-time, not an adapter admission callback. Signed webhook/SDK sender parsing, queues/dedupe/retry, reconnect supervising, credentials/context cursor storage and outbound notification checkpoints were followed statically. WeChat was reviewed through polling, media download/upload, stale context/tokenless fallback, account send serialization, QR/status requests and guarded state persistence.
