docs/review-2026-10-12/validation/original-blank-files-round28/author-static.raw.md:32:The active conversation's separate `useSessionUiAuthority` does consume pendingFirstRun and locally-created IDs. It deliberately uses current project primary for a true draft (`renderer/sessionUiAuthority.ts:53–58,165–185`), and permits project configuration fallback after Main specifically confirms a marked unbound session is absent (`:192–201,256–276`). A real removed root/corrupt state/transport failure is not treated as absence. Existing test source covers that precise contract (`sessionUiAuthority.test.tsx:78–113,116–186`). This protects conversation settings and attachments, but its state is not passed into the panel workspace resolver. The Files normal result instead follows its own actual project fallback described above.
